TITLE:: FluidLoadMultiple
summary:: Join a list of Buffers end to end, like FluidLoadFolder
categories:: Libraries>FluidModel
related:: Classes/FluidLoadFolder, Classes/FluidModel, Classes/FluidLoadStore

DESCRIPTION::
FluidLoadMultiple does for a list of link::Classes/Buffer::s what link::Classes/FluidLoadFolder:: does for a folder of files: it allocates one buffer, copies the buffers into it one after another, and records where each one went in link::#-index::. link::Classes/FluidModel#-build:: uses it when it is given an Array of Buffers.

The buffers must already be loaded, and they must have been read from files: each buffer's file name (code::buffer.path.basename::) becomes its identifier in link::#-index::, so two buffers read from files with the same name overwrite each other's entry, and a buffer without a path (made with code::Buffer.alloc::) causes an error.

warning::
All buffers must have the same number of channels. A buffer with fewer channels than the widest one is not copied, and its part of the joined buffer stays silent.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: files
An Array of loaded link::Classes/Buffer::s.

ARGUMENT:: idFunc
Not used at the moment (kept for compatibility with link::Classes/FluidLoadFolder::).

ARGUMENT:: channelFunc
Not used at the moment.

returns:: A FluidLoadMultiple.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: play
Allocate the joined buffer and copy the buffers into it. Runs in a Routine (forked if needed) and posts its progress.

ARGUMENT:: server
The server. Defaults to link::Classes/Server#*default::.

ARGUMENT:: action
Called with link::#-index:: when all buffers are copied.

METHOD:: files
The Array of source buffers.

METHOD:: buffer
The joined link::Classes/Buffer::.

METHOD:: index
An link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: with one entry per source buffer, keyed by file name. Each entry is an IdentityDictionary with:
definitionlist::
## bounds || code::[startFrame, endFrame]:: of the buffer in the joined buffer
## numchans || its number of channels
## sr || its sample rate
## path || its file path
::

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;

(
~bufs = [
	Buffer.read(s, FluidFilesPath("Tremblay-BeatRemember.wav")),
	Buffer.read(s, FluidFilesPath("Tremblay-SA-UprightPianoPedalWide.wav"))
];  // both stereo
)

(
~loader = FluidLoadMultiple(~bufs);
~loader.play(s, { |index|
	index.keysValuesDo { |name, entry| "% %".format(name, entry[\bounds]).postln };
});
)

{ PlayBuf.ar(2, ~loader.buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~loader.buffer)) * 0.3 }.play;

// the usual way to use it: give the buffers to FluidModel
(
~model = FluidModel(\beatsAndPiano);
~model.build(~bufs, action: { |m| "% slices".format(m.slice_cache.size).postln });
)
::
